Hi all. I'm writing a patch to implement species allies and species enemies
for Rangers.  When a Ranger is created, one monster race is selected randomly
to be the Ranger's species ally, and another monster race is selected to be
the species enemy.

PATCH SPOILER:

Does anyone have other suggestions for what effects this patch should have?
So far, the species enemy will be untameable (taming has no effect).  The
species ally will be peaceful when created, so it will not normally attack
first, but will counterattack.

A few ideas I've rejected as too obvious and unbalancing: Ranger starts with a
tamed monster of the ally species; Ranger auto-tames them; they never attack;
enemy species is always hostile, stalking, or attacks.

I can't release a beta patch right now: I haven't yet coded the random
selection of races (which should be excluded?), or changed the player struct
to record them. I do have a little code in to make the enemy untameable, the
ally peaceful when created, and to re-mark the allied race as peaceful on
restore.

